 "why": "Two answers to an engine sign-in, made the way a box makes them (src/fleet/host/sidecar.js, with src/fleet/crypto.js and src/fleet/seal.js). At the top, one in the clear: the page and the code, signed by the box’s key over the id of the request, as an MCP client is answered. Under `sealed`, one as a phone is answered: the same, with who is signed in, sealed to a key the phone made, whose private half is written here so a phone’s test can open it. Both phones open, check and only then show a code, so both hold that to this file. test/engine-signin-answer.test.js checks it with the box’s own code, and that every change listed breaks the signature. An ECDSA signature and a seal are different each time they are made, so neither can be made again: a test shows they are accepted, and refused once changed.",
